From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:00:50 -0700
Subject: blink: Tolerate a null locale name in LCIDFromLocaleInternal()

Platform::DefaultLocale() is allowed to be empty, and in that case
InitializePlatformLanguage() stores a null AtomicString, so
DefaultLanguage() and therefore the string handed to Locale::Create()
by Locale::DefaultLocale() can be null. The ICU and Mac Locale
implementations cope with that, but on Windows LCIDFromLocaleInternal()
calls String::Is8Bit() on it, which dereferences the null StringImpl
(read at offset 8) the first time a page needs the default Locale, for
example when an <input type=file> builds its shadow tree.

Return 0 for a null or empty name, the same result as for any other
name Windows cannot resolve, so LCIDFromLocale() falls through to its
existing DefaultLanguage() fallback instead of crashing. An empty name
previously reached LocaleNameToLCID(L"") and yielded LOCALE_INVARIANT;
it now takes the same fallback.

Bug: none
Test: blink_platform_unittests --gtest_filter=LocaleWinTest.CreateWithNullLocale
Change-Id: I6f76917d1df827de7256885c5653382072aaa0df
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8266170
Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: David Sanders <dsanders11@ucsbalum.com>
Commit-Queue: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1682959}

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win.cc
index 5e2c006d944ce163a3c96bc407a866033cd2f63c..8634c22aaffcec1327875bb5468dad279a8abb81 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win.cc
@@ -124,8 +124,11 @@ LCID LCIDFromLocaleInternal(LCID user_default_lcid,
   if (DeprecatedEqualIgnoringCase(locale_language_code,
                                   user_default_language_code))
     return user_default_lcid;
-  if (locale.length() >= LOCALE_NAME_MAX_LENGTH)
+  // `locale` is null when the embedder reports an empty default locale; treat
+  // it like any other name that does not resolve.
+  if (locale.empty() || locale.length() >= LOCALE_NAME_MAX_LENGTH) {
     return 0;
+  }
   std::array<UChar, LOCALE_NAME_MAX_LENGTH> buffer;
   auto buffer_slice = base::span(buffer).first(locale.length());
   if (locale.Is8Bit())
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win_test.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win_test.cc
index fc68dff51c879c91e6e54edcaa10cecc04c76d23..98ac153d5dc53e526a4519416c19e2302a58b7f2 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win_test.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/text/locale_win_test.cc
@@ -307,4 +307,9 @@ TEST_F(LocaleWinTest, localizedNumberRoundTrip) {
   TestNumbers(kChineseTW);
 }
 
+TEST_F(LocaleWinTest, CreateWithNullLocale) {
+  std::unique_ptr<Locale> locale = Locale::Create(String());
+  EXPECT_EQ(12u, locale->MonthLabels().size());
+}
